Z||000000||Rodrv6||10-05-2001||09:31 PM||||Well, I've thinned out my car collection somewhat.  My black 84SE with 331,441 miles on the odometer has gone to a new home.  I've had it since early 84 when I bought it new.  A young couple in our church had a real need for a second car, and since I'm single and had 4 cars sitting around here, I felt like I needed to help them out.  I'll be able to keep an eye on it since I told them to bring it back to me if it has any maintennance needs.  I can honestly say I've gotten my money's worth out of it over the years!  I still have my 88 GT, a Nissan Maxima, and a Porsche 911, so fun driving is still a priority  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I guess I'll have to change my signature as soon as I come up with a better one.<BR>I did a total teardown and rebuild on the SE back in 1998 (all the way down to a bare space frame), and found no real problems other than normal wear on suspension parts and a rusty battery box.  Just goes to show that with regular maintennance these cars will last a loooooong time!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
